  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "A seat usually runs 'metasystem work build' from inside its goal worktree. When it does, the new design check appends its warning line to that worktree's git-tracked narrator digest (metasystem/records/narrator-digest.log) before the builder starts. The unit runner then records the builder's change as the whole worktree diff against the base commit, so every first build of a tier-2 or tier-3 unit that draws a warning carries an edit to a shared control file that the builder did not make. A warning is drawn when the goal has no accepted design, when its critique line is missing (which, by the design's own count, is true of all 11 designs accepted before this gate), when the critique is still open, or when the check cannot run. That edit goes into the unit's reviewed and proven diff and into the unit commit, and from there to main. In short, the change ships wrong behaviour into every gated build's subject. The gate itself works without a fix, but it is not safe: it silently changes what other work is judged on.",
      "evidence": "Traced path at the reviewed tree. (1) cmd/metasystem/intent.go:691-703: selectRoot takes the layout from the invocation's working directory and sets inv.stateRoot to RootForInstallation(layout.InstallationRoot). In a template checkout, internal/stateroot/stateroot.go:145-151 returns the installation itself, which is <goal worktree>/metasystem. (2) cmd/metasystem/intent_work.go:855-878: goalWorktree accepts any worktree, including the current one, that has goal/G checked out. The goal goal-worktree-dispatch-uses-the-primary records that seats dispatch builder rounds from goal worktrees. (3) cmd/metasystem/intent_work.go:630-636: the wrapped prepare calls recordDesignGate before the run starts. intent_design_gate.go recordDesignGate calls o.digest(inv.stateRoot, entry, now) whenever the warning line is not empty. (4) internal/narratordigest/digest.go:70-84,158-188: AppendWithLayoutReader writes <installation>/records/narrator-digest.log, which git ls-files lists as tracked (metasystem/records/narrator-digest.log). (5) internal/launch/unit_run.go:604-617: writeDiff and WorktreeDiff call worktreeDiff(worktree, base) with no exclusions. Line 662 runs git add -A over the whole worktree, so the digest edit becomes part of the unit's recorded change. The design itself avoids the digest in the reset lane checkout because it is 'a tracked file' (section 2, the lane), but it does not handle the goal worktree. The tests cannot show the defect because the work bench puts its worktree (parent/work) in a different folder from its state root (intent_work_test.go:175-180). The behaviour is still present at the branch tip (intent_design_gate.go:192).",
      "id": "F-1-BUILD-DIGEST-LINE-ENTERS-UNIT-DIFF",
      "material": true,
      "severity": "medium"
    }
